{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/exigents/337966-so-why-are-they-called-exigents","id":337966,"title":"So why are they called Exigents?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Exalted","Exigents"],"posts":[{"date":"2014-12-12T05:26:23-08:00","id":337966,"title":"So why are they called Exigents?","content":"Title really says it all. I tried looking up the word and I don't see an immediate connection. Surely something requiring immediate aid or attention is less long term than an Exaltation call for, right? Am I missing something?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1521-jang","name":"Jang","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1521_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"228"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-12T05:34:44-08:00","id":337993,"title":"","content":"When a God is in severe need it seeks access to the Exigence, a spiritual mecahnisism set up by the Sun which allows them to produce an Exalt at the great cost. Where 'great cost' can include the entire dissolution of the God in question. It's not something they do for giggles, which is where it gets it's name <br /> <br /> Exigetn Exalted, as a group, take their name from the Exigence from which they all arose On the other hand Exigents are diverse enought that they're probably not spoken of as a group anywhere outside of Heaven, amoung those who know how these things are done. To anyone else the idea that Strawmaden Janest and the Chosen of Masks could be the same sort of being on some level is rediculous.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1849-suddenthunder","name":"SuddenThunder","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1849_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"563"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-12T07:31:59-08:00","id":338060,"title":"","content":"I wouldn't generally go in for the &quot;being immortal means you regard things as taking a shorter time&quot; bit, but I might be inclined a little bit towards it in terms of a crisis that requires a one-off (and possibly no more long lived) Exalt could be regarded as urgent or immediate even over the span of a mortal lifetime.<br /> <br /> Although mostly I think the word is just to allude to the idea that there's an issue of this as power given out as an emergency response, without being fully confined to it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-12T09:49:51-08:00","id":338113,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>SuddenThunder</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/exigents/337966-so-why-are-they-called-exigents?p=337993#post337993\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Exigent Exalted, as a group, take their name from the Exigence from which they all arose On the other hand Exigents are diverse enought that they're probably not spoken of as a group anywhere outside of Heaven, amoung those who know how these things are done. To anyone else the idea that Strawmaden Janest and the Chosen of Masks could be the same sort of being on some level is rediculous.</div> </div> </div> </div>I dunno; in that hours-long dev-and-writer video I recall them discussing the likelihood of Great Forks suffering a veritable shitstorm of &quot;heroes&quot; when word of the resurgence of the Exigence gets out, with most of the wanna-be &quot;Chosen&quot; not understanding that the gods of Great Forks won't necessarily be able to grant them the divine fire.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>He/him","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","name":"TheCountAlucard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar177_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10857"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-12T10:33:58-08:00","id":338140,"title":"","content":"The Flame of Exigence is handed down from the Unconcquered Sun from on high to a god that has petitioned for it and found worthy. It allows for gods to create their own Exigents. They are not known as the Exigent Exalted, just Exigents, or specifically their own kind of Exalted. Strawmaiden Janest is a Harvest Exalted, which is an Exigent.<br /> <br /> The Exigence is something of a last resort, as it requires great sacrifice from the god/gods that use it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/393-godjaw","name":"Godjaw","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar393_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"665"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-12T10:44:20-08:00","id":338167,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Godjaw</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/exigents/337966-so-why-are-they-called-exigents?p=338140#post338140\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The Flame of Exigence is handed down from the Unconcquered Sun from on high to a god that has petitioned for it and found worthy.</div> </div> </div> </div>Or sometimes stolen and/or passed around to create an unspeakable multi-themed abomination that is the son of many gods.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Chicanery-No: If a player uses this Charm in an abusive or exploitative manner, the ST may punch him right in the goddamn face.&quot; --TheDementedOne<br /> <br /> &quot;Happiness is <i>very</i> brittle and short-lived in the Exalted community, because <i>ressentiment</i> is our cultural touchstone.&quot; --Gayo","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3420-zelbinnean","name":"Zelbinnean","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3420_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5884"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-12T12:55:49-08:00","id":338280,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TheCountAlucard</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/exigents/337966-so-why-are-they-called-exigents?p=338113#post338113\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I dunno; in that hours-long dev-and-writer video I recall them discussing the likelihood of Great Forks suffering a veritable shitstorm of &quot;heroes&quot; when word of the resurgence of the Exigence gets out, with most of the wanna-be &quot;Chosen&quot; not understanding that the gods of Great Forks won't necessarily be able to grant them the divine fire.</div> </div> </div> </div>No one in Creation is going to learn &quot;hey, the Exigence, which is the source of miraculous power that lets the lesser gods bestow Exaltations, seems to be having a resurgence.&quot; They're going to hear rumors, myths, and legend. They'll listen to stories about a harvest god blessing a farm girl with the power to fend off a shambolic legion of Fae, about a deadly warrior-poet who draw divine might from a sword forged by one of the gods, about a thief who stole a god's most treasured possession and wagered it back for unimaginable power. You might see droves of heroes heading towards Great Forks, but they'll be doing it because they believe the gods will confer great and heroic blessings upon them, not because they know the first things about Exigents.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Developer for Exalted<br /> <br /> Want to write for Exalted? Look at the <a href=\"http://theonyxpath.com/submission-guidelines/\" target=\"_blank\">freelancer submission guidelines.</a><br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/user?u=451515\" target=\"_blank\">Robert Vance's Patreon</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":13}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/527-robert-vance","name":"Robert Vance","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar527_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10044"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-12T13:34:24-08:00","id":338355,"title":"","content":"And of course, none among the Immaculate Faithful will believe Exigents to be Exalted at all, Exigent or otherwise.<br /> <br /> Janest and the other sporadic and eclectic Chosen will be regarded as god-blooded, or the beneficiaries of unusual divine blessings, or possibly gods themselves fooling around in the guise of mortals.<br /> <br /> Thankfully, almost none of them will be regarded as Anathema, since everyone knows Anathema wear the forms of beasts, bear blasphemous glowing marks upon their foreheads, and radiate the stolen light of the moon or sun.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>formerly Tornado Wolf, formerly Inugami","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","name":"Sunder the Gold","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar636_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5515"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-12T13:36:34-08:00","id":338356,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TheCountAlucard</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/exigents/337966-so-why-are-they-called-exigents?p=338113#post338113\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I dunno; in that hours-long dev-and-writer video I recall them discussing the likelihood of Great Forks suffering a veritable shitstorm of &quot;heroes&quot; when word of the resurgence of the Exigence gets out, with most of the wanna-be &quot;Chosen&quot; not understanding that the gods of Great Forks won't necessarily be able to grant them the divine fire.</div> </div> </div> </div>At least there'll always be room to party. METE LEAF AND QAT FOR EVERYONE~","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Won't you believe in him? Even if there is no God, or Buddha...there is still Kamen Rider.&quot; \u2014Taki Kazuya, <i>Kamen Rider SPIRITS</i><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#008000\">Now...count up </span><span style=\"color:#4B0082\">all your sins.</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/160-cyclonejoker","name":"CycloneJoker","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar160_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"713"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-12T13:49:38-08:00","id":338368,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sunder the Gold</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/exigents/337966-so-why-are-they-called-exigents?p=338355#post338355\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">And of course, none among the Immaculate Faithful will believe Exigents to be Exalted at all, Exigent or otherwise.<br /> <br /> Janest and the other sporadic and eclectic Chosen will be regarded as god-blooded, or the beneficiaries of unusual divine blessings, or possibly gods themselves fooling around in the guise of mortals.<br /> <br /> Thankfully, almost none of them will be regarded as Anathema, since everyone knows Anathema wear the forms of beasts, bear blasphemous glowing marks upon their foreheads, and radiate the stolen light of the moon or sun.</div> </div> </div> </div>Pretty sure that is incorrect, they will totally accept that there are other exalts besides the Dragon Blooded and Exigents will be one of the kinds they accept as exalts.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Exalted Whose Name is Carved in Leaves of Jade<br /> Senator of the Greater Chamber<br /> Champion of the Silver Pact<br /> Chosen of the Little Gods<br /> Agent of Fate","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/988-mizu","name":"Mizu","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar988_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1520"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-12T13:56:16-08:00","id":338372,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mizu</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/exigents/337966-so-why-are-they-called-exigents?p=338368#post338368\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Pretty sure that is incorrect, they will totally accept that there are other exalts besides the Dragon Blooded and Exigents will be one of the kinds they accept as exalts.</div> </div> </div> </div>I could have sworn Sunder had it right, that only DBs are considered &quot;Exalted&quot; in-setting by the Immaculates. They don't know about Sidereals; Anathema aren't Exalted, they're body-jumping sorcerer-demons; Exigents are champions of gods but spiritually inferior to the Dragon-Blooded.<br /> <br /> And Exigents may well have caste marks and almost assuredly will have anima banners, but as they won't be Solar/Lunar caste marks and sunlight/moonlight animas, the Wyld Hunt doesn't really care about them from a &quot;spiritually corrupt&quot; standpoint.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Chicanery-No: If a player uses this Charm in an abusive or exploitative manner, the ST may punch him right in the goddamn face.&quot; --TheDementedOne<br /> <br /> &quot;Happiness is <i>very</i> brittle and short-lived in the Exalted community, because <i>ressentiment</i> is our cultural touchstone.&quot; --Gayo","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3420-zelbinnean","name":"Zelbinnean","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3420_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5884"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-12T14:03:40-08:00","id":338395,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mizu</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/exigents/337966-so-why-are-they-called-exigents?p=338368#post338368\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Pretty sure that is incorrect, they will totally accept that there are other exalts besides the Dragon Blooded and Exigents will be one of the kinds they accept as exalts.</div> </div> </div> </div>The Immaculate Faith preaches that the Exalted are the Princes of the Earth, the Dragon-Blooded are the Exalted Princes of the Earth, and that your goal in life should be to live righteously so that you are rewarded with reincarnation as an Exalt, and then eventually to join the Immaculate Dragons in Heaven.<br /> <br /> Exigents have no place in this worldview. They cannot be Exalted, because they cannot be Heaven's reward for righteous living, because they are not Dragon-Blooded Princes of the Earth.<br /> <br /> And if any of that reasoning seems circular to you, it's the same way in-setting.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>formerly Tornado Wolf, formerly Inugami","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","name":"Sunder the Gold","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar636_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5515"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-12T14:15:53-08:00","id":338404,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sunder the Gold</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/exigents/337966-so-why-are-they-called-exigents?p=338395#post338395\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The Immaculate Faith preaches that the Exalted are the Princes of the Earth, the Dragon-Blooded are the Exalted Princes of the Earth, and that your goal in life should be to live righteously so that you are rewarded with reincarnation as an Exalt, and then eventually to join the Immaculate Dragons in Heaven.<br /> <br /> Exigents have no place in this worldview. They cannot be Exalted, because they cannot be Heaven's reward for righteous living, because they are not Dragon-Blooded Princes of the Earth.<br /> <br /> And if any of that reasoning seems circular to you, it's the same way in-setting.</div> </div> </div> </div>As I understand it having been said, the defintions of Anathema will be recast a bit so that it more specifically applies to Solar and Lunar Exalted in 3e. Your entire statement is based on previous edition takes on a 3e-exclusive entity. <br /> <br /> And stuff.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>And stuff.<br /> <sub><a href=\"https://blaqueandstuff.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My DeviantArt Page</a> // <a href=\"http://blaqueandstuff.tumblr.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My tumblr</a> // <a href=\"http://www.dropbox.com/sh/trxegr5hl27s1l5/AAAegBBzxbDhvk1YpYJqdhz8a?dl=0\" target=\"_blank\">Exalted 3e Houserules</a></sub>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/353-blaque","name":"Blaque","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar353_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2976"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-12T14:23:25-08:00","id":338433,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Blaque</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/exigents/337966-so-why-are-they-called-exigents?p=338404#post338404\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> As I understand it having been said, the defintions of Anathema will be recast a bit so that it more specifically applies to Solar and Lunar Exalted in 3e. Your entire statement is based on previous edition takes on a 3e-exclusive entity.<br /> <br /> And stuff.</div> </div> </div> </div>Where did I say that the Immaculate Faith considers anything other than Celestial Exalted to be Anathema? I said the exact opposite.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>formerly Tornado Wolf, formerly Inugami","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","name":"Sunder the Gold","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar636_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5515"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-12T14:25:35-08:00","id":338434,"title":"","content":"I seem to recall one of the Devs saying that the Immaculate Faith will view Exigents largely in the same light as God-blooded. That is to say, they're the result of improper congress between gods and man, but that doesn't mean they can't be useful.<br /> <br /> Edit: Found it. Holden said it. It's in the Exigent section of the What We Know wiki. Can't quote it directly since I'm on my mobile.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":155,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/155-noodle","user":"Noodle","date":". 12-12-2014, 05:27 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/155-noodle","name":"Noodle","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar155_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1415"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-12T14:25:39-08:00","id":338435,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mizu</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/exigents/337966-so-why-are-they-called-exigents?p=338368#post338368\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Pretty sure that is incorrect, they will totally accept that there are other exalts besides the Dragon Blooded and Exigents will be one of the kinds they accept as exalts.</div> </div> </div> </div>Dragon-Blooded don't have any reason to think of &quot;Exalted&quot; as a category separate from Dragon-Blooded. They and they alone are the Princes of the Earth.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Developer for Exalted<br /> <br /> Want to write for Exalted? Look at the <a href=\"http://theonyxpath.com/submission-guidelines/\" target=\"_blank\">freelancer submission guidelines.</a><br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/user?u=451515\" target=\"_blank\">Robert Vance's Patreon</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":10}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/527-robert-vance","name":"Robert Vance","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar527_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10044"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-12T14:30:07-08:00","id":338439,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sunder the Gold</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/exigents/337966-so-why-are-they-called-exigents?p=338355#post338355\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">And of course, none among the Immaculate Faithful will believe Exigents to be Exalted at all, Exigent or otherwise.<br /> <br /> Janest and the other sporadic and eclectic Chosen will be regarded as god-blooded, or the beneficiaries of unusual divine blessings, or possibly gods themselves fooling around in the guise of mortals.<br /> <br /> Thankfully, almost none of them will be regarded as Anathema, since everyone knows Anathema wear the forms of beasts, bear blasphemous glowing marks upon their foreheads, and radiate the stolen light of the moon or sun.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> We don't quite know what Immaculate's think of Exigents, but we do know is that it's regarded as illegal conduct between gods and humans. They may very well consider them Exalted.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/393-godjaw","name":"Godjaw","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar393_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"665"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-12T14:56:45-08:00","id":338480,"title":"","content":"Man, a lot of people on this thread are interested in what Lookshy's particular religion thinks of Exigents, aren't they? <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/tongue.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Stick Out Tongue\" smilieid=\"5\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> As big and wide-spanning as the Realm and its satrapies are, I'd think that one would be more curious about the Immaculate <i>Philosophy</i>'s opinion. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>He/him","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","name":"TheCountAlucard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar177_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10857"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-12T15:05:25-08:00","id":338489,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Godjaw</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/exigents/337966-so-why-are-they-called-exigents?p=338439#post338439\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">We don't quite know what Immaculate's think of Exigents, but we do know is that it's regarded as illegal conduct between gods and humans. They may very well consider them Exalted.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, not really, see Vance's statement below <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Chicanery-No: If a player uses this Charm in an abusive or exploitative manner, the ST may punch him right in the goddamn face.&quot; --TheDementedOne<br /> <br /> &quot;Happiness is <i>very</i> brittle and short-lived in the Exalted community, because <i>ressentiment</i> is our cultural touchstone.&quot; --Gayo","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3420-zelbinnean","name":"Zelbinnean","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3420_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5884"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-12T15:44:50-08:00","id":338519,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Jang</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/exigents/337966-so-why-are-they-called-exigents#post337966\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Title really says it all. I tried looking up the word and I don't see an immediate connection. Surely something requiring immediate aid or attention is less long term than an Exaltation call for, right? Am I missing something?</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm pretty sure it is just the fact that Exigents are created due to acute and desperate needs, as you say. My reading (which may be wrong, as we don't have much information) is that they're generally meant to be for things that the god needs to deal with but can't, since the Principle of Diminishment is such a harsh constraint for an immortal being. Like, I think the idea is that if it's <i>not</i> a dire circumstance the UCS will tell you to piss off? In principle, I guess the UCS could just show up in person and fix the problem for you, but the fact that that doesn't happen should probably be taken as a setting conceit related to the game's premise, rather than a comment on the nature of Exigents.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":104,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/104-gayo","user":"Gayo","date":". 12-12-2014, 06:48 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/104-gayo","name":"Gayo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar104_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1948"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-12T15:50:28-08:00","id":338521,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Gayo</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/exigents/337966-so-why-are-they-called-exigents?p=338519#post338519\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Like, I think the idea is that if it's <i>not</i> a dire circumstance the UCS will tell you to piss off?</div> </div> </div> </div>Well one problem with the Exigence is that however it works has to account for both Black Market and Dirty Bomb scenarios being possible. Which implies a lower level of control since no way in hell would UCS willingly hand the Exigence to the Leech Gods, but it seems like they should be able to bargain in Heaven's slums for an &quot;unimprinted&quot; goblet of Exigence Fire or whatever.<br /> <br /> Maybe this works by a god receiving the Exigence, but then not using it, instead selling it on the Black Market to be bought by the highest bidder. Which to me implies imperfect record-keeping, since this kind of racket sounds to be at least a little commonplace and good record-keeping/oversight (&quot;Amoth, this is the third Exigence you've acquired in the last decade, mind splainin?&quot;) would largely prevent it from happening.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Chicanery-No: If a player uses this Charm in an abusive or exploitative manner, the ST may punch him right in the goddamn face.&quot; --TheDementedOne<br /> <br /> &quot;Happiness is <i>very</i> brittle and short-lived in the Exalted community, because <i>ressentiment</i> is our cultural touchstone.&quot; --Gayo","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3420-zelbinnean","name":"Zelbinnean","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3420_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5884"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-12T15:59:20-08:00","id":338524,"title":"","content":"I'd say that there are individuals like Mnemon who are able to see past the same sorts of logical incongruities behind excluding Exigents as they do for Solars and Lunars, even if they still think the ultimate reason for that exclusion is sound. I'd also say that even for ones who don't recognise other Exalted, somebody who has the sort of power that an Exigent would, they're recognised as a measure above more &quot;typical&quot; kinds of blessing, even if they're not all seen as the same kinds of people.<br /> <br /> There is that line about how Exigents who are in active rebellion against the Immaculate Order are viewed as Anathema, but since that also refers to various other beings, that appears to be a categorization for the sake of our recognition, rather than an internal one. To them, it's just people empowered by gods towards nefarious ends. Maybe it's even a matter of theological debate as to whether or not the ones who are opposing them are ontologically distinct from ones who don't, rather than having a moral or ideological difference as guided by personal agency.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-12T17:41:17-08:00","id":338577,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Zelbinnean</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/exigents/337966-so-why-are-they-called-exigents?p=338521#post338521\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Well one problem with the Exigence is that however it works has to account for both Black Market and Dirty Bomb scenarios being possible. Which implies a lower level of control since no way in hell would UCS willingly hand the Exigence to the Leech Gods, but it seems like they should be able to bargain in Heaven's slums for an &quot;unimprinted&quot; goblet of Exigence Fire or whatever.<br /> <br /> Maybe this works by a god receiving the Exigence, but then not using it, instead selling it on the Black Market to be bought by the highest bidder. Which to me implies imperfect record-keeping, since this kind of racket sounds to be at least a little commonplace and good record-keeping/oversight (&quot;Amoth, this is the third Exigence you've acquired in the last decade, mind splainin?&quot;) would largely prevent it from happening.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, but it sounds like you need to explain why you <i>should</i> get an Exigence, and that presumably involves an exigency.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/104-gayo","name":"Gayo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar104_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1948"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-12T18:44:10-08:00","id":338606,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Blaque</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/exigents/337966-so-why-are-they-called-exigents?p=338404#post338404\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> As I understand it having been said, the defintions of Anathema will be recast a bit so that it more specifically applies to Solar and Lunar Exalted in 3e. Your entire statement is based on previous edition takes on a 3e-exclusive entity.<br /> <br /> And stuff.</div> </div> </div> </div>Actually, the term is being recast so that, while yes, Exigents will not <i>automatically</i> be targets of Wyld Hunts just for being <i>rival </i>exalts, some <i>could </i>be declared Anathema on a case by case basis.<br /> <br /> From the Wyld Hunt preview a while back, it seems that while Immaculates will no longer be using the term &quot;Anathema&quot; to simply mean &quot;all exalted other than the dragon-blooded&quot;, they'll be using it for the <i>anything</i> they find abhorrent to a prosperous and proper life; that is still all Solar and Lunar exalted of course, but also sometimes rakasha, demons, beastmen, god blooded, elementals, and gods (and their Exigents) who are declared to be operating in <i>opposition</i> to Immaculate beliefs. (For the Immaculate Order, that includes opposition to Realm interests.)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/487-greyman","name":"Greyman","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar487_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1308"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-12T18:45:22-08:00","id":338607,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Zelbinnean</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/exigents/337966-so-why-are-they-called-exigents?p=338521#post338521\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Well one problem with the Exigence is that however it works has to account for both Black Market and Dirty Bomb scenarios being possible. Which implies a lower level of control since no way in hell would UCS willingly hand the Exigence to the Leech Gods, but it seems like they should be able to bargain in Heaven's slums for an &quot;unimprinted&quot; goblet of Exigence Fire or whatever.<br /> <br /> Maybe this works by a god receiving the Exigence, but then not using it, instead selling it on the Black Market to be bought by the highest bidder. Which to me implies imperfect record-keeping, since this kind of racket sounds to be at least a little commonplace and good record-keeping/oversight (&quot;Amoth, this is the third Exigence you've acquired in the last decade, mind splainin?&quot;) would largely prevent it from happening.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> It's probably more a case, where God A petitions the Unconquered Sun for an Exigence, perhaps under false pretenses, perhaps not. Then for whatever reason, it doesn't get used by the God in question. Perhaps the situation resolved itself before they could, or they were waylaid by another God and the Exigence was stolen. Then, the process happens again with a different God.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/370-oriares","name":"Oriares","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar370_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"404"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-12T19:07:22-08:00","id":338622,"title":"","content":"Also possible that exigence is occasionally given to gods who are believed trustworthy to prepare for bad situations. Maybe sometimes it gets done like a fire extinguisher and its just there with the hope that it doesn't have to get used. It could also get delivered in to a god when the situation is perceived as bad enough. Either of those cases allows for an exigence to get stolen as well as the possibility of it getting thrown on the black market because the god turned out to be less trustworthy than previously believed.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3400-nalak42","name":"nalak42","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3400_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2931"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-12T19:53:05-08:00","id":338638,"title":"","content":"In general, I imagine it's much like shards. The idea of power never being confined to a host or recipient transit vessel 24/7. If you have the superpowerful essence, Lytek's tools, etc. Then you can nab whatever it is. I have no idea WHAT it takes to steal Exigence, just thinking that if you need Lytek's tools in addition to superpowerful essence (So I'd assume, I mean this is never explicitly stated but you figure you'd have to be crazy powerful on a mystic level to grab a shard of all things. Just as a general concept of what shards are capable of empowering people to do.) then you can steal a shard and perform jiggerypokery on it until it does what you want. Exigence, for whatever means of transmission it has, clearly has a falliable system for transmisison as the shards do. Maybe it's ripped out of an exigent's corpse an instant after they die, before their soul can even pass through the lethe. Maybe it's... I dunno, grabbed in-between Yu-Shan and the god in question who wants to use it. Maybe the god -sells- their exigence after successfully petitioning Sol for it by some kind of divine loophole.<br /> <br /> Regardless, Yu-Shan is far from perfect. I don't think record-keeping is going to cut it when despite massive personal cost, a nuclear option is crazy useful as a bargaining chip. It's got to be a hard thing to get, even for that reason.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2532-blitzkitty","name":"BlitzKitty","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2532_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"72"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-13T10:13:04-08:00","id":339191,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Robert Vance</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/exigents/337966-so-why-are-they-called-exigents?p=338280#post338280\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">No one in Creation is going to learn &quot;hey, the Exigence, which is the source of miraculous power that lets the lesser gods bestow Exaltations, seems to be having a resurgence.&quot; They're going to hear rumors, myths, and legend. They'll listen to stories about a harvest god blessing a farm girl with the power to fend off a shambolic legion of Fae, about a deadly warrior-poet who draw divine might from a sword forged by one of the gods, about a thief who stole a god's most treasured possession and wagered it back for unimaginable power. You might see droves of heroes heading towards Great Forks, but they'll be doing it because they believe the gods will confer great and heroic blessings upon them, not because they know the first things about Exigents.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm playing a D&amp;D (Pathfinder) game. We're level 10, we've wandered into a dungeon filled with CR14 encounters (mostly demons). Last session, on the way to the CR23 boss fight, we encountered a Paladin. Thinking said Paladin would save our bacon, we welcomed him into our group. He died 18 seconds (combat time) later. Turns out he was only level 6. (As an aside, I'm playing again tomorrow -- if anyone has any advice on not to be horribly butchered by a Balor Lord, pitch me a PM.)<br /> <br /> One thing I liked about 2nd was being able to call charms by their names and being able to call a diaklave a diaklave. I'm sure that a mythic world of storytelling and mystery will be a great setting for Exalted Novels, but when I ST 3rd I'ma gonna <i>explictly</i> tell my players &quot;This is an Essence 2 Exigent with diaklave using Melee Excellency&quot;. Because the meta is what makes the game work.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/899114-the-official-exalted-forum-introduction-thread?p=899399#post899399\" target=\"_blank\">Hi, I'm JohnDoe244</a>. My posts represent my opinions, not facts.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/531-johndoe244","name":"JohnDoe244","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar531_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2958"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-13T11:00:24-08:00","id":339227,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>JohnDoe244</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/exigents/337966-so-why-are-they-called-exigents?p=339191#post339191\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm playing a D&amp;D (Pathfinder) game. We're level 10, we've wandered into a dungeon filled with CR14 encounters (mostly demons). Last session, on the way to the CR23 boss fight, we encountered a Paladin. Thinking said Paladin would save our bacon, we welcomed him into our group. He died 18 seconds (combat time) later. Turns out he was only level 6. (As an aside, I'm playing again tomorrow -- if anyone has any advice on not to be horribly butchered by a Balor Lord, pitch me a PM.)<br /> <br /> One thing I liked about 2nd was being able to call charms by their names and being able to call a diaklave a diaklave. I'm sure that a mythic world of storytelling and mystery will be a great setting for Exalted Novels, but when I ST 3rd I'ma gonna <i>explictly</i> tell my players &quot;This is an Essence 2 Exigent with diaklave using Melee Excellency&quot;. Because the meta is what makes the game work.</div> </div> </div> </div>It has nothing to do with &quot;meta,&quot; it's just a fact of the setting. Most people in Creation don't know anything about the Exigence, and may not have reason to sort the various divinely-empowered Exigents they've encountered into the same ontological bucket. Conversely, the Sidereal Exalted know a great deal about the Exigence and Exigents, and probably have at least a fair grasp of some of the rules the process operates under.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Developer for Exalted<br /> <br /> Want to write for Exalted? Look at the <a href=\"http://theonyxpath.com/submission-guidelines/\" target=\"_blank\">freelancer submission guidelines.</a><br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/user?u=451515\" target=\"_blank\">Robert Vance's Patreon</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/527-robert-vance","name":"Robert Vance","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar527_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10044"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-13T11:11:47-08:00","id":339232,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Robert Vance</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/exigents/337966-so-why-are-they-called-exigents?p=339227#post339227\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It has nothing to do with &quot;meta,&quot; it's just a fact of the setting. Most people in Creation don't know anything about the Exigence, and may not have reason to sort the various divinely-empowered Exigents they've encountered into the same ontological bucket. Conversely, the Sidereal Exalted know a great deal about the Exigence and Exigents, and probably have at least a fair grasp of some of the rules the process operates under.</div> </div> </div> </div>To echo this, we've also been told that lay people really don't understand or care that Elementals are different from Fair Folk or demons or gods. They classify the creatures they encounter with more practical categories.<br /> <br /> If it shows no faculty for language or civilized discourse, it's a beast. If it eats their livestock and neighbors, it's a monster. If it can be propitiated for mercy or blessings with offerings and prayers, it's a god.<br /> <br /> While not taxonomically correct, these boxes are no less valid and true.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>formerly Tornado Wolf, formerly Inugami","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","name":"Sunder the Gold","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar636_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5515"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-13T11:33:01-08:00","id":339239,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Robert Vance</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/exigents/337966-so-why-are-they-called-exigents?p=339227#post339227\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It has nothing to do with &quot;meta,&quot; it's just a fact of the setting. Most people in Creation don't know anything about the Exigence, and may not have reason to sort the various divinely-empowered Exigents they've encountered into the same ontological bucket. Conversely, the Sidereal Exalted know a great deal about the Exigence and Exigents, and probably have at least a fair grasp of some of the rules the process operates under.</div> </div> </div> </div>Kind of a weird example ot this for me is some stuff in biology. I think for most people, lots of animals are just weird animals, like oysters, squid, snails, and such. They don't htink of them at all in relation wiht one-another, they're just there. Biologists know they're all molluscs, have a common ancestor, and are actually possible variants on some same body plan and get all interested into that stuff. For most normal people a snail is just..a snail. Not a mollusc.<br /> <br /> And stuff.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>And stuff.<br /> <sub><a href=\"https://blaqueandstuff.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My DeviantArt Page</a> // <a href=\"http://blaqueandstuff.tumblr.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My tumblr</a> // <a href=\"http://www.dropbox.com/sh/trxegr5hl27s1l5/AAAegBBzxbDhvk1YpYJqdhz8a?dl=0\" target=\"_blank\">Exalted 3e Houserules</a></sub>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/353-blaque","name":"Blaque","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar353_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2976"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-13T12:32:01-08:00","id":339308,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Blaque</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">Biologists know they're all molluscs</div> </div> </div> </div> I was about to correct this, and then remembered that I keep mixing up the term mollusc and crustacean. <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Blaque</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">For most normal people a snail is just..a snail</div> </div> </div> </div> I myself get a huge kick out of the fact that the arms of a cephalopod are a specialized form of the characteristic foot of the slug and snail. I'm... <i>technically</i> not a biologist.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-13T12:32:33-08:00","id":339309,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>JohnDoe244</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/exigents/337966-so-why-are-they-called-exigents?p=339191#post339191\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm playing a D&amp;D (Pathfinder) game. We're level 10, we've wandered into a dungeon filled with CR14 encounters (mostly demons). Last session, on the way to the CR23 boss fight, we encountered a Paladin. Thinking said Paladin would save our bacon, we welcomed him into our group. He died 18 seconds (combat time) later. Turns out he was only level 6. (As an aside, I'm playing again tomorrow -- if anyone has any advice on not to be horribly butchered by a Balor Lord, pitch me a PM.)</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes actually, because it's the advice I've given to players in exalted, D&amp;D and other games.<br /> <br /> If there is a big scary thing that is almost impossible to defeat standing there waiting for you to fight it... Don't Fight It. Instead do this thing called Running Away. It works wonders for keeping characters alive.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Odd_Canuck is not a topical medication or food product and is not to be taken internally or seriously.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/31-odd_canuck","name":"Odd_Canuck","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar31_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1474"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-13T12:36:52-08:00","id":339333,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>JohnDoe244</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/exigents/337966-so-why-are-they-called-exigents?p=339191#post339191\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Thinking said Paladin would save our bacon, we welcomed him into our group. He died 18 seconds (combat time) later. Turns out he was only level 6.</div> </div> </div> </div>Isn't there anyone with Detect Magic in that group of yours? Realizing he only had one or two magic items should have been something of a hint. I consider it standard to make a rough guesstimate of NPCs I encounter based on their gear. And if I want to know the Essence level of that Exigent, I use All-Encompassing Sorcerer's Sight.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/815-kazorh","name":"Kazorh","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar815_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"900"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-13T12:38:44-08:00","id":339337,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Kazorh</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/exigents/337966-so-why-are-they-called-exigents?p=339333#post339333\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">And if I want to know the Essence level of that Exigent, I use All-Encompassing Sorcerer's Sight.</div> </div> </div> </div>I doubt effects like AESS are going to be so uber/easy to get all relevant information in 3e.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Chicanery-No: If a player uses this Charm in an abusive or exploitative manner, the ST may punch him right in the goddamn face.&quot; --TheDementedOne<br /> <br /> &quot;Happiness is <i>very</i> brittle and short-lived in the Exalted community, because <i>ressentiment</i> is our cultural touchstone.&quot; --Gayo","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3420-zelbinnean","name":"Zelbinnean","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3420_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5884"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-13T12:42:06-08:00","id":339338,"title":"","content":"I reason that Exigent is derived from &quot;Exalted Gentle(wo)man&quot; in the First Age it was tradition to offer to tip one's hat to such individuals and offer to take their coat even if they didn't have one and try to marry off your daughter to them regardless of their gender.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"https://swordofcreation.net/\" target=\"_blank\">Sword of Creation</a> a hub for Exalted related content</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7-lioness","name":"Lioness","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7_2.png","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5443"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-13T12:47:08-08:00","id":339343,"title":"","content":"Besides, &quot;An Essence 2 Exigent with a Daiklave using a Melee excellency&quot; is not all that useful. Exigents vary a lot, so that doesn't really tell you anything about the limits of their capabilities. Besides, assuming system transparency is still in place, the players would already have superior information than that, such as exact dice pools and other relevant mechanical effects","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>You need a picture altered to fit your Exalted character, or just looking for some visual inspiration? Check out the twice-reborn <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/266-photoshop-exaltification\" target=\"_blank\"> Exaltification thread</a>. And here is my <a href=\"http://danelsan.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">Deviantart page</a><br /> <br /> S\u00f8ren Kierkegaard + Kim Kardashian = <a href=\"https://twitter.com/KimKierkegaard\" target=\"_blank\">Brilliance</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/868-danelsan","name":"danelsan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar868_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1492"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-13T13:19:26-08:00","id":339370,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/exigents/337966-so-why-are-they-called-exigents?p=339308#post339308\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> I was about to correct this, and then remembered that I keep mixing up the term mollusc and crustacean. I myself get a huge kick out of the fact that the arms of a cephalopod are a specialized form of the characteristic foot of the slug and snail. I'm... <i>technically</i> not a biologist.</div> </div> </div> </div>Actually, it isn't. Which is kind of freaky. THey're just extensions of the head. The foot is actually what turned into the little nozzle thingy they use to do jet propulsion.<br /> <br /> And stuff.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>And stuff.<br /> <sub><a href=\"https://blaqueandstuff.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My DeviantArt Page</a> // <a href=\"http://blaqueandstuff.tumblr.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My tumblr</a> // <a href=\"http://www.dropbox.com/sh/trxegr5hl27s1l5/AAAegBBzxbDhvk1YpYJqdhz8a?dl=0\" target=\"_blank\">Exalted 3e Houserules</a></sub>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/353-blaque","name":"Blaque","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar353_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2976"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}